<answer> 

Let's simplify the expression for $f(x)$:

\begin{align*}
f(x) &= \dfrac{5x + 1}{x - 1}\\
&= (5 + \dfrac{6}{x-1})
\end{align*}

Now, we substitute $x = 7$ into the simplified expression for $f(x)$:

\begin{align*}
f(7) &= 5 + \dfrac{6}{7-1} \\
&= 5 + \dfrac{6}{6} \\
&= 5 + 1 \\
&= \boxed{6}
\end{align*}
Therefore, the value of $f(7)$ is 6.

